# Deceiver Exarch has flash (CR 702.8): Bot1 casts it in Bot2's upkeep. Its enters trigger is modal (CR 700.2a): Bot1 chooses
# "Tap target permanent an opponent controls" as it goes on the stack, and that mode's target is a permanent Bot2 controls - not
# one of Bot1's own Islands (the refusal; Bot2's Island is the control). As it resolves Bot2's Island is tapped (CR 701.26a).
# The Exarch is a 1/4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Island
Mox Sapphire
Deceiver Exarch
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Pearl
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot1.Hand.Deceiver Exarch.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Island)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Deceiver Exarch.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Deceiver Exarch.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Deceiver Exarch.Keywords = Flash
